Hi tpm2 mailing list,

I=E2=80=99m new here, so I briefly introduce myself. I am Florian, working =
at Siemens in Germany.
I am currently on charge to implement a TPM V2 (Infineon slb9670, SPI conne=
cted) on our custom board, named =E2=80=98LPE9403=E2=80=99, equipped with a=
n processor 64-bit ARM NXP LS1043a.

I already made some adjustment (defconfig in U-Boot and Linux, device tree,=
 init code in U-Boot).
I have installed =E2=80=9Ctpm2-tools=E2=80=9D using =E2=80=98apt-get instal=
l=E2=80=99. I get to the point where the TPM is correctly detected and I ca=
n use some of the function like tpm2_getrandom().

However, when I execute the command =E2=80=98reboot=E2=80=99, it leads ever=
y time to a kernel panic. The logs seems to indicate that something went wr=
ong with the shutdown of the TPM.

Can you provide me support to fix this issue ?


My config :
- Processor 64-bit ARM NXP LS1043a
- TPM V2 Infineon slb9670
- tpm2-tools: Version: 3.1.3-2
- linux kernel version: 4.19.144

I provide with this mail a zip archive =E2=80=98debug_logs.zip=E2=80=99 con=
taining :
- =E2=80=98linux_logs.txt' : logs from Linux startup + kernel panic on rebo=
ot
